<%# Not Last.fm's logo. Redrawing somebody's trademark from memory gets you a
    mangled trademark, and theirs is a wordmark that does not survive being 16
    pixels wide — so this says what the thing does instead: the bars of the
    equalizer, which are already the app's mark for a song being heard, going out
    of the house. Last.fm's own name is on the words beside it, and their
    attribution is on the door below. %>
<span aria-hidden="true"
      class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-[#b90000] text-white">
  <svg class="size-3.5" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
    <rect x="1" y="9" width="2.5" height="5" rx="1"/>
    <rect x="5" y="5.5" width="2.5" height="8.5" rx="1"/>
    <rect x="9" y="2" width="2.5" height="12" rx="1"/>
    <path d="M13.6 2.3a.9.9 0 0 1 1.27.1 5.4 5.4 0 0 1 0 6.9.9.9 0 1 1-1.37-1.16 3.6 3.6 0 0 0 0-4.58.9.9 0 0 1 .1-1.26Z"/>
  </svg>
</span>
